---
description: Testing discipline — pytest + asyncio + VCR; cassettes-as-contract; coverage floor.
globs: ["tests/**/*.py", "src/strata_forge/**/*.py"]
alwaysApply: false
---

- Every new code path gets a test in the same PR.
- Unit tests (`tests/unit/<module>/`) are fast and offline — the default home for a new test. Mock at
  the seam (LiteLLM, fsspec, the Langfuse SDK). Heavy optional SDKs (`asyncssh`, `sky`, `trl`,
  `transformers`) are injected as fakes through `sys.modules` so the suite runs on a bare install.
- `tests/integration/` holds cross-module tests: the `test_cross_module.py` files need no services,
  the `integration`-marked ones need `make stack-up`. `tests/e2e/` imports every file under
  `examples/` and `notebooks/` and is what catches drift between them and the public API — fix it
  when it fires, never skip it.
- `make test` runs the unit suite; `make test-all` runs everything and is what you run before a PR
  that moves the public API.
- Provider-touching tests use VCR cassettes (`tests/vcr/cassettes/<provider>/<scenario>.yaml`).
  Recording requires `RECORD=1` plus live keys; CI replays with `record_mode="none"`. Tests skip
  gracefully when the matching cassette is absent.
- VCR cassettes MUST scrub API keys, AWS signatures, and GCP tokens via the `before_record_request`
  filter in `tests/vcr/conftest.py`. Inspect the produced YAML before committing — a leaked
  credential must be rotated.
- Live tests (`@pytest.mark.live`) are env-gated and run only nightly. Never on PR.
- Coverage: one package-wide floor of 85 % line coverage (`fail_under` in `pyproject.toml`), measured
  by CI over `tests/unit`. `llm/`, `core/`, and `config/` are held to a higher bar by convention —
  treat a drop there as a regression even though no per-module gate enforces it. Never lower the
  floor to make a build pass.
- No skipped tests without a tracking issue link in the skip reason.
- Snapshot tests (`syrupy`) cover provider schema serialization and token accounting — a failing
  snapshot is an early-warning signal. Read the diff and re-record deliberately; never regenerate to
  get green.
- Property tests (`hypothesis`) exist for cache keys, tokenization, metrics, and prompt rendering.
  Extend them rather than replacing a property with an example when a counterexample shows up.
- Pytest markers: `live`, `redis`, `slow`, `integration` — declared in `pyproject.toml`. New markers
  go there (`--strict-markers` is on).
- `asyncio_mode = "auto"` — async tests don't need `@pytest.mark.asyncio`.
- Never weaken an assertion, a threshold, or a type to make a test pass. A red check is information.
